# Where the dashboard reads from.
#
# Unset (the usual case for a public demo): the dashboard serves
# web/src/demo/snapshot.json, a recording of five real runs, and says so on
# every page. Nothing needs to be deployed alongside it.
#
# Set: every page reads that ReLab control plane instead, on the server during
# rendering. The browser never sees this value and never talks to the API
# directly, so it may point at a host that is not publicly routable — but it
# must be reachable from wherever the dashboard runs, which on Vercel means
# from Vercel's network.
#
# RELAB_API_TOKEN is the bearer token this dashboard sends. A control plane
# with RELAB_API_TOKENS configured rejects requests without one; a loopback
# deployment with no tokens needs nothing here. Use a viewer token: the
# dashboard reads and never writes.
#
# The token is read on the server during rendering and never reaches the
# browser, but it is still a shared password for the whole read API — keep it
# in the deployment's secret store, never in this file or in a commit.
#
# RELAB_API_URL=http://localhost:8080
# RELAB_API_TOKEN=
